From e279725e0960e21a7a4bace8a0b60a99f0947cb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 15:08:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(shepherd): address CodeRabbit stability findings on the
 watch loop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- watch.js: make the cadence sleep abortable — defaultSleep now races the timer
  against ctx.signal, so SIGINT/SIGTERM stops the loop at once instead of waiting
  out the current jittered interval (~72s). Timer + abort listener both cleaned up.
- watch.js: make the watcher claim atomic — the watcherRunning check and writePid
  now run TOGETHER inside the cross-process journal lock (defaultClaim), so two
  concurrent starts can never both claim and emit duplicate NDJSON.
- watch-lifecycle.js: attach a no-op 'error' listener to the detached child, so an
  async spawn error (ENOENT/EACCES after return) can never become an unhandled
  exception that crashes ship.

Tests: abortable-sleep (already/mid-abort + normal timer), concurrent atomic
claim (exactly one wins), EventEmitter child emitting 'error' post-return.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/pr-monitor/watch-lifecycle.js       |  5 +++
 lib/pr-monitor/watch.js                 | 48 ++++++++++++++++++----
 test/pr-monitor/watch-lifecycle.test.js | 15 +++++++
 test/pr-monitor/watch.test.js           | 54 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 114 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

